      "id": "2117262655681429743",
      "text": "When you do the math based on $hg $hgraf guidence on capex and opex you see they are set to have massive margins. \n\nThe interesting thing is that their pure 100% sp2 bonding Turbostatic fractal graphene out performs competitors by 10x to 100x.  So you’re using 10th or less the material.   Consistent and no agglomeration.  \n\nSo what this means is when they charge $250k a tonne. That would be like $25k a tonne.  The rest of the industry is still struggling to try to get all in costs down to $50k a tonne. So it’s like half price vs competitors. \n\nThis gives me comfort and begs the question… how quickly can they ramp up and how disruptive could they become.  Could they not potential bankrupt competitors with their pricing power and dominate globally?\n\nI think it’s worth while to read all the science studies on the material and do the math.  Do your own due diligence and decide for yourselves.  Just my thoughts….",
